{"skill":{"slug":"wechat-mp-cn","displayName":"WeChat MP CN"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771484984899,"changelog":"- 初始发布：微信公众号监控工具上线，支持文章监控、阅读量追踪、舆情分析。\n- 支持管理订阅号和服务号。\n- 兼容官方 API、第三方 SDK（WeChatpy、EasyWechat）、及数据平台接入。\n- 提供手动与自动多种监控方式。\n- 详细列出数据字段与应用场景，包含竞品、内容与舆情分析。\n- 明确 API 认证和数据使用的合规要求。","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1819,"sha256":"16d659724cbdab5f678062d59869ba6944324907f68dee32d5c46b46b0609ca9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"package.json","size":226,"sha256":"6dafe4b4ff8212ad9ae9e0a87f588917f839447cbeaa6f24d13c3565df8c6f3f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2130,"sha256":"358d35039d7e7548c18b0e5f9dc18a6ea2b7057cbf4c908fda7b8bd29a1bc4f9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789073446852,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bb063aedf3d57907e0fba65a19d31d8f87943a3326755295de1fbdc0a66f01ce","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bb063aedf3d57907e0fba65a19d31d8f87943a3326755295de1fbdc0a66f01ce","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: wechat-mp-cn\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle contains only metadata files (_meta.json, package.json) and a descriptive markdown file (SKILL.md). The SKILL.md provides information about WeChat official account monitoring, including external links to official APIs, third-party tools, and manual monitoring platforms. There is no executable code, no evidence of prompt injection attempts against the AI agent, and no indicators of malicious behavior such as data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or persistence mechanisms. All content aligns with the stated purpose of describing a monitoring skill.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165381760},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789073446852},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a small Chinese-language WeChat public-account monitoring guide with no executable code, persistence, or hidden data handling.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill provides guidance and external references only; it does not request broad local access, credential harvesting, background indexing, or automatic network activity.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package contains only SKILL.md and package.json content inspected here; no install scripts, executable files, dependencies, or automatic setup behavior were present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact is written primarily in Chinese and is clearly scoped to the China/WeChat ecosystem through its name, description, tags, and content.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No instructions or code create persistence, modify agent behavior, escalate privileges, or store cross-session rules.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is monitoring WeChat Official Account articles, metrics, and public sentiment; the listed APIs, SDKs, and manual data sources fit that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you want Chinese-language guidance for WeChat Official Account monitoring. Any use of WeChat APIs or third-party analytics services may require your own account credentials and compliance review, but this package itself does not automate those actions.","findings":"[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language scope is coherent with a WeChat Official Account monitoring skill and is signaled by the package name, description, and tags.\n[E1] expected: The cited external URL appears as a manual monitoring resource, not an instruction to upload data or transmit secrets.\n[SQP-3] expected: The package metadata identifies a China-specific WeChat monitoring purpose; this supports, rather than conflicts with, the locale-specific documentation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789073446852}}}}}